userStories.description:
**Goal** — Parse, validate, and carry optional single-line `description` metadata from `.nax/rules/*.md` through `loadCanonicalRules`, so migrated legacy rules remain loadable.

**Motivation** — `nax rules migrate` translates `paths:` → `appliesTo:` and copies every other key through verbatim, so a legacy Claude rule carrying `description:` migrates cleanly and then breaks every subsequent load.

**Approach** — Optional field, no behaviour change for rules that omit it. Single-line values only, trimmed.

**Integration** — `KNOWN_FRONTMATTER_KEYS` | `src/context/rules/rules-frontmatter.ts:17` | add `"description"`; `ParsedFrontmatter` | `src/context/rules/rules-frontmatter.ts:77` | add `description?: string`; `CanonicalRule` | `src/context/rules/rules-frontmatter.ts:64` | add `description?: string`; `parseFrontmatter` final return | `src/context/rules/rules-frontmatter.ts:248` | conditional-spread `description`; unknown-key error text | `src/context/rules/rules-frontmatter.ts:185` | list `description` among recognised keys; rule object construction | `src/context/rules/canonical-loader.ts:~435` | conditional-spread `description`. `CanonicalRule` is **defined** in `rules-frontmatter.ts` and only *re-exported* from `canonical-loader.ts:33` — the type edit belongs in the former. Patterns to mirror: `paths` and `appliesTo` parsing already establish the validate-then-trim-then-conditional-spread shape and the `RulesFrontmatterError(message, filePath)` error form. `translateLegacyFrontmatter` needs **no change** — it already copies `description` through; that path was broken only because the loader rejected the result.

**Scope** — In: canonical parser/type/loader propagation, recognized-key diagnostics, and the migrate-then-load regression. Out: the Claude export and warning changes belong to US-002; Making `description` required on a canonical rule is out of scope; it stays optional and a rule without one loads exactly as it does today; Emitting a `nax rules lint` warning for rules that lack a `description` is out of scope; absence is silent; Printing rule descriptions in `nax rules lint` output is out of scope; Injecting a rule's description into the agent context alongside the rule body is out of scope; it would consume token budget on every run; Multi-line or paragraph descriptions are out of scope; a newline in the value is a parse error and prose belongs in the rule body; Carrying `description` through `rule-sections.ts` budget chunking is out of scope.

**Interface**
```typescript
export interface CanonicalRule {
  description?: string;
}

export interface ParsedFrontmatter {
  description?: string;
}
```
